  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Flood Risk Mitigation and Early Action for Vulnerable Populations in White Nile, Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">White Nile State is likely to face severe flooding between 17&#x2013;19 August 2025, with over an 85% probability due to high river discharge levels and above-average rainfall. Historical data from 2020&#x2013;2023 shows similar floods causing significant damage and disease outbreaks. The anticipated 2025 flooding is expected to cause cholera and malaria outbreaks, loss of shelter and livelihoods, access bottlenecks, and overwhelmed health systems. This intervention leverages the presence and acceptance of consortium partners in the targeted communities, ensuring rapid implementation and trust-based access, and aligns with Start Fund&#x2019;s guidance on anticipatory action to minimize residual risk and strengthen preparedness.</narrative>
  </description>
